[{:db/id "q-109712/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "5b2450fb-1253-5afd-9c31-e9e5f1892df7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109712/selection/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" :answer/id #uuid "0de66c21-a952-5a1a-816b-9b5a223870ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109712/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "b3043c8e-4860-53bc-b1a6-e1ba31a60e98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109712/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "19c49a1a-f217-551f-a8d3-1391bd5418d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109712/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "53657f4a-00fe-5925-af62-d0b432ad1e9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109712/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98403821-c63f-5312-bc66-d2288f3ae9e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109712/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer-field/choices ["q-109712/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" "q-109712/selection/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" "q-109712/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-109712/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-109712/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109712" :question/id #uuid "8262518f-3842-5651-b1d9-5224332846b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109712" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2{v}^{2})^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{4}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{v}^{2}}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the substitution \n\n$$\nw={v}^{2}+1\\,⇒\\,\\text{d}w=2v\\,\\text{d}v,\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{w}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{w}^{3}}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}-\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109712/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109712"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779/selection/c71471265c459db429c0904073d51b98263c5556bf8642fd8ee00873955333bc" :answer/id #uuid "a4ab9932-a696-50ea-ba06-0ca34c418293" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779/selection/5557d3ddff38fb0dc3e0bd4afbed5c096a6dd7f35140075b4c7b00425ed68942" :answer/id #uuid "1b3960d8-7920-5e18-98ed-63fbbe8b2d8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779/selection/240ec3d8434c02553987bfbb2f37ed146250c7b9acb5a5e9aab45f367730d44d" :answer/id #uuid "15eb8a3d-99ac-5d9d-b785-caebb6467dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779/selection/5498cb0ba3ada570cc4b5ab398a9b4ae1f792c194fb1ebad7f93f82c7ce158a4" :answer/id #uuid "93359eb9-e1fb-5a74-9793-f9fe879052d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "47ea83d0-43e8-5134-8b7b-bc6355bfbb89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3147e495-7d19-5002-8291-82ed7f374d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109779/selection/5557d3ddff38fb0dc3e0bd4afbed5c096a6dd7f35140075b4c7b00425ed68942" :answer-field/choices ["q-109779/selection/c71471265c459db429c0904073d51b98263c5556bf8642fd8ee00873955333bc" "q-109779/selection/5557d3ddff38fb0dc3e0bd4afbed5c096a6dd7f35140075b4c7b00425ed68942" "q-109779/selection/240ec3d8434c02553987bfbb2f37ed146250c7b9acb5a5e9aab45f367730d44d" "q-109779/selection/5498cb0ba3ada570cc4b5ab398a9b4ae1f792c194fb1ebad7f93f82c7ce158a4" "q-109779/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109779" :question/id #uuid "815c0ebb-2900-5353-8633-596c7a148310" :question/math-academy-id "q-109779" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9},\n$$\n\nof radius $3.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\pi \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947/selection/5d18c3f3c994eebc2e9790e8920c1fa31d20d4dff0485f241f85b22c191fb983" :answer/id #uuid "0c6efc79-d2da-5ca1-b556-85a3d66178eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947/selection/1aecb459bbdf1868d3b3e9b10a760d24ae3c2e3ff5a041b671361b7af824362b" :answer/id #uuid "e16daed2-33c8-5909-b9c0-371e5e772c68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947/selection/b0d1e917686537fa1529c3ba84e76157551038de385e4d2a69439ff625b01635" :answer/id #uuid "d027da9f-d814-5a71-a484-b43e9aeaedb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947/selection/4b6797352858a161fcf775e4df39dd415b7211278b070c678e0ca85776249f13" :answer/id #uuid "8d975feb-30c1-5948-97ec-435f2d64de14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947/selection/e5c8696d1ca684c6a4a75d8ad96cbe7d0659e9760c894a6e0a6334a24315c9fe" :answer/id #uuid "ba916f02-4de2-5c79-b898-b64bc286ffce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7b55fd-b82e-5f75-822d-3acaf71a687e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109947/selection/b0d1e917686537fa1529c3ba84e76157551038de385e4d2a69439ff625b01635" :answer-field/choices ["q-109947/selection/5d18c3f3c994eebc2e9790e8920c1fa31d20d4dff0485f241f85b22c191fb983" "q-109947/selection/1aecb459bbdf1868d3b3e9b10a760d24ae3c2e3ff5a041b671361b7af824362b" "q-109947/selection/b0d1e917686537fa1529c3ba84e76157551038de385e4d2a69439ff625b01635" "q-109947/selection/4b6797352858a161fcf775e4df39dd415b7211278b070c678e0ca85776249f13" "q-109947/selection/e5c8696d1ca684c6a4a75d8ad96cbe7d0659e9760c894a6e0a6334a24315c9fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109947" :question/id #uuid "c235bda4-b647-59f5-b137-7fc5bc86576a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109947" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,3{u}^{2},\\,u-v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6u & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}6u & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6u \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6u)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{u}^{2}+4+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72{u}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4(18{u}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109947/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2928b0de-fadb-5ffa-b30f-72c0051f0ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109947"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019/selection/2f27eb4ef5eab58ea874531a85bc7107efed317ca984db270320aacdb88a3adb" :answer/id #uuid "f1841cb9-4fe4-5be6-9833-0d8f9fe14e8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019/selection/28ff31260d8e9834817d6ae51ec55326fe22dc116c9aa26221dabe4f44c13227" :answer/id #uuid "d70a39aa-ebe3-59ff-95cf-f411247ec22f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+2{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019/selection/9c4d3fd9db995655e2f9123d1892d36b83d1092c5bcd58100f238f33a2a7181a" :answer/id #uuid "892c7308-216a-5e53-a41d-7a77e9a8411d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019/selection/5cad18bb732eb3650eff84f26ef11b77a07aac17a9b3dd8de20eb38443bfbdab" :answer/id #uuid "8ff38a2d-91b8-55a0-a461-dbc862a6f2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019/selection/e5d32dbfa9fa70712d435a427e6d3b21e6396d59420043d838192d76cabf1738" :answer/id #uuid "006665c0-81fe-5182-b96e-b397e502be0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "44d0792e-e8ad-5d54-9112-a313ab29bd78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110019/selection/9c4d3fd9db995655e2f9123d1892d36b83d1092c5bcd58100f238f33a2a7181a" :answer-field/choices ["q-110019/selection/2f27eb4ef5eab58ea874531a85bc7107efed317ca984db270320aacdb88a3adb" "q-110019/selection/28ff31260d8e9834817d6ae51ec55326fe22dc116c9aa26221dabe4f44c13227" "q-110019/selection/9c4d3fd9db995655e2f9123d1892d36b83d1092c5bcd58100f238f33a2a7181a" "q-110019/selection/5cad18bb732eb3650eff84f26ef11b77a07aac17a9b3dd8de20eb38443bfbdab" "q-110019/selection/e5d32dbfa9fa70712d435a427e6d3b21e6396d59420043d838192d76cabf1738"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110019" :question/id #uuid "8e92a306-a654-5aa7-ab29-bbc8c19240b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110019" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u{sin}^{2}⁡v-2u{cos}^{2}⁡v,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2u)^{2}+(2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡v+16{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}(1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110019/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2928b0de-fadb-5ffa-b30f-72c0051f0ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110019"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551/selection/db879806e556bb7ec6146c2f9614e542893e7420217cfaee0202c7b4d8ce7e8f" :answer/id #uuid "aa6aae1a-f572-598c-8055-af1e416c81d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551/selection/c6ac502c9e763c7cbd44071bda009f59f59b31c6253188048f297291992ede66" :answer/id #uuid "6dddbe0e-4670-5ac3-8684-c435dbad81d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551/selection/3dacb0d8773b9724a5c0a4c26a2612c1f947f51e375046a9ea0886399520844a" :answer/id #uuid "dc2527f7-f87d-5b85-96a4-f80bcb61f858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551/selection/e41e3f0585fddeb9e398df455d5cc948bf1b0ed4be9a5cd84a3cfd4180724786" :answer/id #uuid "e68da096-1bc8-507c-b87b-540b40ec16b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{35}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551/selection/9226826ae7eb80db0aeb289f37a1aa2976eee547903b8cfd11e7d6a1ab52ffb0" :answer/id #uuid "996e152e-a39d-554a-a0ac-f231c507eda0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fd3b6d2-68e8-5bf5-bcad-8a3b3c8df0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110551/selection/e41e3f0585fddeb9e398df455d5cc948bf1b0ed4be9a5cd84a3cfd4180724786" :answer-field/choices ["q-110551/selection/db879806e556bb7ec6146c2f9614e542893e7420217cfaee0202c7b4d8ce7e8f" "q-110551/selection/c6ac502c9e763c7cbd44071bda009f59f59b31c6253188048f297291992ede66" "q-110551/selection/3dacb0d8773b9724a5c0a4c26a2612c1f947f51e375046a9ea0886399520844a" "q-110551/selection/e41e3f0585fddeb9e398df455d5cc948bf1b0ed4be9a5cd84a3cfd4180724786" "q-110551/selection/9226826ae7eb80db0aeb289f37a1aa2976eee547903b8cfd11e7d6a1ab52ffb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110551" :question/id #uuid "ed5a0c57-61d7-5283-bf59-b2f0b08e70f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-110551" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,u+2v,\\,2u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,-1,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-5,\\,-1,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1},\n$$\n\nof radius $1.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{35}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi \\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110551/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
